159
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:31.740
Guess what, everybody?
大家猜怎么着？

160
00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.160
I don't know a lot about golfing.
我对高尔夫了解不多。

161
00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.880
This is why I'm quiet because I'm like, I don't know.
这就是我保持安静的原因，因为我心想，我也不懂啊。

162
00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:38.780
But here's the big kicker.
但重点来了。

163
00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:41.380
And this is why I think you and I need to go to this golf course.
这就是为什么我觉得你和我得去这个高尔夫球场看看。

164
00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:41.900
Okay.
好吧。

165
00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.300
They have something called foot golf.
他们有一种叫“足球高尔夫”的项目。

166
00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:45.460
Foot golf?
足球高尔夫？

167
00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.060
I'd never heard of it.
我从没听说过。

168
00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.240
It's a real thing.
这是真实存在的。

169
00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.040
It's a combination of soccer and golf.
它是足球和高尔夫的结合体。

170
00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:52.280
And hacky sack.
还有沙包球。

171
00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:54.860
I think you could hacky and sack it in there.
我觉得你可以在里面玩沙包球。

172
00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:59.260
There's basically a special golf course, but the holes are really big
基本上就是有一个专门的高尔夫球场，但球洞非常大，

173
00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:02.180
and you kick the ball down the course into the hole.
你把球踢进球道里的洞里就行。

174
00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:02.920
Okay.
好吧。

175
00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:03.880
Foot golf.
足球高尔夫。

176
00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.760
Maybe we could frolf and then foot golf.
也许我们可以先玩飞盘高尔夫，再玩足球高尔夫。

177
00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:12.020
I would foot golf if there was like a pony keg set up on like the eighth hole.
如果第八洞那里设个小桶装啤酒，我就愿意玩足球高尔夫。

178
00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:16.080
So like you kick your ball, then you have a beer, then you kick your ball.
就是踢一脚球，喝口啤酒，然后再踢一脚。

179
00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.420
What's a pony keg?
什么是小桶装啤酒？

180
00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.680
A pony keg, isn't that?
小桶装啤酒，不是吗？

181
00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:19.980
Don't y'all have pony kegs?
你们都没听说过小桶装啤酒吗？

182
00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:20.900
It's like a party keg.
就像派对用的那种小桶。

183
00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:22.520
It's like a mini keg of beer.
就是迷你啤酒桶。

184
00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:23.380
A pony keg?
小桶装啤酒？

185
00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:23.700
Anyone?
有人知道吗？

186
00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:24.760
Sam?
萨姆？

187
00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:25.480
Cassie?
凯西？

188
00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:26.120
Pony keg?
小桶装啤酒？

189
00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:26.720
Ever heard of it?
听说过吗？

190
00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.440
A pony keg is a mini keg?
小桶装啤酒就是迷你桶？

191
00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:30.080
Yeah.
对。

192
00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.220
It's like a baby keg.
就像婴儿桶一样。

193
00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:31.780
No, you're right.
不，你说得对。

194
00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.260
Pony keg is a quarter keg.
小桶装啤酒就是四分之一桶。

195
00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:33.540
Yeah.
对。

196
00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:34.420
Thank you.
谢谢。

197
00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.580
What's a half keg called?
那半桶装叫什么？

198
00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:39.230
Silence.
沉默。

199
00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:44.940
I don't find any cool names.
我没找到什么酷炫的名字。

200
00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:46.920
Oh, so you can get up.
噢，所以你可以起来了。

201
00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.120
Here are your choices.
这是你的选择。

202
00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.140
Pony keg, half keg, keg.
小桶、半桶、大桶。

203
00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:56.820
I feel like they sell more pony kegs just because the name is cute, but I don't know.
我觉得他们卖出更多小桶纯粹是因为名字可爱，但我也不确定。

204
00:07:56.820 --> 00:08:00.500
And you can carry them if you're on the petite side, like myself.
而且如果你像我一样娇小，还能拎得动它们。

205
00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.860
Oh, we're learning so much today.
噢，我们今天学到了好多。

206
00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:03.680
So much.
真的好多。

207
00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.520
Fast fact number three.
冷知识第三条。

208
00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:10.800
Angela, you were very, very, very pregnant in this episode.
安吉拉，这一集里你怀孕的程度非常、非常、非常明显。

209
00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.680
Yeah, I was.
没错，确实是。

210
00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:19.420
When you were filming your scenes with Dwight in the office, Lee Eisenberg had the flu.
当你和德怀特在办公室拍戏时，李·艾森伯格得了流感。

211
00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:20.560
He was not there that day.
那天他不在现场。

212
00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:22.600
Only Gene Stepnitsky was on the set.
只有吉恩·斯泰普尼茨基在片场。

213
00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:27.560
When they got into the editing bay to edit the episode, Lee Eisenberg was there and he
当他们进入剪辑室剪辑这一集时，李·艾森伯格也在，他

214
00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:31.680
said, you guys, why don't we have any wider shots of these scenes?
说，伙计们，为什么这些场景没有更广的镜头？

215
00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:38.480
And Dave Rogers and Gene had to remind him because Angela's belly was very hard to hide.
戴夫·罗杰斯和吉恩不得不提醒他，因为安吉拉的肚子实在太难遮了。

216
00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:44.640
So all of these, all of these shots are like Angela from like the shoulders up.
所以所有这些镜头，基本上都是安吉拉肩膀以上的特写。

217
00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:47.700
But here is what else I found in my Googling, Angela.
但安吉拉，我谷歌的时候还发现了别的事。

218
00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:48.620
What?
什么？

219
00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:53.040
By the time this episode aired, you had given birth.
这一集播出的时候，你已经生完孩子了。

220
00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:54.420
I know.
我知道。

221
00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:58.420
You gave birth five days before this episode aired.
你是在这一集播出前五天生的孩子。

222
00:08:58.760 --> 00:08:59.700
That is true.
确实如此。

223
00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.400
Well, lady, I have a really fun story from this episode.
好吧，女士，关于这一集我有个特别有趣的故事。

224
00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.520
And it's something that involves the golf course.
而且和高尔夫球场有关。

225
00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:10.180
I had no scenes at the golf course, but I went to visit the fellas.
我在高尔夫球场没有戏份，但我去探望了那帮伙计们。

226
00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:15.240
I was doing a whole series at this time on NBC.com called Adventures with Angela.
当时我正在 NBC.com 上做一个系列节目，叫《安吉拉的冒险》。

227
00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:19.760
And Creed and Ed had written a song for my baby.
克里德和埃德为我的宝宝写了一首歌。

228
00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:23.540
I mean, with the banjo, the guitar, the whole thing.
我是说，用班卓琴、吉他，整套装备都带上了。

229
00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:27.540
So I went to the golf course on Monday on their lunch.
所以周一午餐时间我去了高尔夫球场。

230
00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:31.480
And we sat out in this beautiful green, like grassy area.
我们坐在那片美丽的绿色草地上。

231
00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.540
And they sang to me.
他们为我唱了歌。

232
00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:38.080
And not only that, I couldn't remember how we got there.
不仅如此，我都不记得我们是怎么过去的了。

233
00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:41.380
I was like, I don't remember driving to this place or where it was.
我就像，我不记得开车去过那个地方，也不记得它在哪。

234
00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.740
And you know, when you're a passenger, how you don't really pay attention as much.
你知道的，当你坐副驾时，通常不会太留意路况。

235
00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:45.340
Yeah.
是啊。

236
00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:50.660
So I found this email that I had written to John Krasinski, where I said,
所以我翻到了我写给约翰·卡拉辛斯基的一封邮件，上面写着：

237
00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.700
Hey, John, I'll see you Monday.
嘿，约翰，周一见。

238
00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:53.580
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

239
00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:55.900
Creed is picking me up in a sports car.
克里德要开跑车来接我。

240
00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:56.960
Should I be scared?
我该害怕吗？

241
00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.760
And we're going to come and have lunch.
我们要去吃午饭。

242
00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:02.180
And he and Ed are going to sing a song for my little baby.
他和埃德要为我的小宝宝唱首歌。

243
00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:06.120
Oh, so you wrote in Creed's sports car?
噢，所以你是坐克里德的跑车去的？

244
00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.520
I wrote in Creed's little two-seater sports car.
我是坐克里德那辆双座小跑车去的。

245
00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:11.820
And they sang this song to me.
他们为我唱了那首歌。

246
00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.560
And it was on NBC.com.
而且还发在了 NBC.com 上。

247
00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:14.880
And Jenna, they gave me a copy.
珍娜，他们给了我一份拷贝。

248
00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:19.060
And I tore my house up looking for this this week.
这周我把家里翻了个底朝天在找它。

249
00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:21.920
I have ransacked the whole house.
我把整个房子都搜遍了。

250
00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:23.860
I know I have it somewhere.
我知道它肯定在某处。

251
00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:25.900
And I really wanted to play it for you guys.
我真的很想放给你们听。

252
00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:30.260
But Joya, who worked with us over at NBC.com, is on the case.
不过在NBC.com和我们共事的乔亚正在处理这件事。

253
00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.360
She's going to find it.
她会把它找出来的。

254
00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:35.940
And hopefully, maybe in a revisited, I'll be able to play it for you guys, because it's
希望在回顾节目里，我能有机会放给你们听，因为它

255
00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:36.680
really special.
真的很特别。

256
00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:39.020
And I'm just heartbroken that I couldn't find it.
没能找到它，我真是心碎极了。

257
00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:41.660
That is so cool, Angela.
那太酷了，安吉拉。

258
00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.900
I remember seeing the video of that.
我记得看过那个视频。

259
00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:45.820
So I really do hope you find it.
所以我真心希望你能找到它。

260
00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:46.720
Me too.
我也是。

261
00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:47.400
Me too.
我也是。

262
00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:48.160
It was so cute.
那真的太可爱了。

263
00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:51.240
I remember Creed started off with, Angela's baby.
我记得克里德开头说的是，安吉拉的宝宝。

264
00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.360
It was just so fun.
那真的太有趣了。

265
00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:56.440
Well, and that's really all I had for this.
好吧，关于这个我只有这些要说的了。

266
00:10:56.560 --> 00:11:00.960
I guess I have something that could be considered half a fast fact that I could throw in there.
我想我有一个勉强算得上半个快讯的小料可以加进去。

267
00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.520
Half a fast fact?
半个快讯？

268
00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:03.180
What you got?
你有什么料？

269
00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:08.740
My half a fast fact is that Toby was not in this episode because he was busy writing the
我的半个快讯是，托比没出现在这一集里，因为他当时正忙着写

270
00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:09.500
season finale.
季终集。

271
00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.080
Ooh, that is a good one.
噢，那确实是个好料。

272
00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:14.040
Well, I have a little Kinsey tidbit.
好吧，我有一个关于金赛的小花絮。

273
00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:17.260
Ooh, guess who found her script of job fair?
噢，猜猜谁找到了她的《招聘会》剧本？

274
00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:18.660
This lady.
就是本人。

275
00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:20.060
Oh my gosh, Angela.
天哪，安吉拉。

276
00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:23.700
This is very exciting to me because I have a couple of fan questions that I didn't know
这让我非常兴奋，因为我有几个粉丝提问我之前不知道

277
00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:25.820
the answer to, but I bet the answers are in the script.
答案，但我敢打赌答案就在剧本里。

278
00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:27.180
Ooh, let me get it.
噢，让我去拿一下。

279
00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:27.660
I'll get it.
我去拿。

280
00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:31.480
And let's go to break and we'll come back and jump into some job fair.
我们先休息一下，回来后就开始聊《招聘会》这一集。

281
00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:32.660
I like it.
我喜欢这个主意。

282
00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:44.640
All right, we are back.
好了，我们回来了。

283
00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:48.240
I have my script of job fair and Jenna right out of the gate.
我拿到了我的《招聘会》剧本，珍娜，开门见山。

284
00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:49.700
I have a question for you.
我有个问题要问你。

285
00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:50.600
What is it?
什么问题？

286
00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:54.340
Did you notice that this episode does not have a cold open?
你注意到这一集没有冷开场了吗？

287
00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:56.240
I kind of did, Angela.
我确实注意到了，安吉拉。

288
00:11:56.500 --> 00:12:00.320
We have a scene before the credits, but it's on plot.
我们在片头字幕前确实有一场戏，但那是关于剧情的。

289
00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:01.460
It's on story.
是关于故事本身的。

290
00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:05.560
It's not one of those standalone comedic cold opens that we're used to.
它不是那种我们习惯的独立喜剧冷开场。

291
00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:06.640
I did notice.
我确实注意到了。

292
00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:07.300
That's right.
没错。

293
00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:09.640
We just kind of get right into the meat of the episode, right?
我们直接进入了这一集的正题，对吧？

294
00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:10.300
Yes.
是的。

295
00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:13.900
There was a cold open and I'm going to read you a little bit about what it was.
其实原本是有个冷开场的，我来给你们读一下那是关于什么的。

296
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:14.200
Okay.
好的。

297
00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:14.900
Okay.
好的。

298
00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:21.980
So in the cold open, you hear the screaming noise from the men's restroom and everyone in
在那个冷开场里，你能听到男厕所传来的尖叫声，然后办公区里的每个人

299
00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.200
the bullpen kind of grumbles like, oh, not again.
都抱怨说，噢，又来了。

300
00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:26.640
And Michael comes out.
接着迈克尔走了出来。

301
00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:31.640
He's just exasperated because he has dropped everything that was in his pockets into the
他只是因为把口袋里的所有东西都掉进了

302
00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:31.980
toilet.
马桶里而感到恼火。

303
00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:32.940
Like everything.
真的是所有东西。

304
00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:33.900
He lists it off.
他一一列举了出来。

305
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:39.700
He dropped his cell phone, his tip calculator, his wallet, his white strips, candy corn, his
他把手机、小费计算器、钱包、牙齿美白贴、玉米糖、

306
00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:40.200
eraser.
橡皮擦都掉进去了。

307
00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:42.480
And then Jim says, what about your car keys?
然后吉姆问，那你的车钥匙呢？

308
00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:45.460
And Michael says, I threw them into the toilet out of anger.
迈克尔说，我一生气就把它们扔进马桶里了。

309
00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:49.760
And this leads him to this light bulb moment.
这让他灵光一现。

310
00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:55.320
Cause I guess this happens quite frequently for Michael and he goes into his office and
我想这种事对迈克尔来说经常发生，他走进办公室，

311
00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:59.340
he comes out and he's like, guys, I have invented this amazing invention.
出来后就说，伙计们，我发明了一个了不起的东西。

312
00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:03.800
And he says, it's the mesh toilet guard to go over the toilet.
他说，这是一个套在马桶上的网状马桶防护罩。

313
00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:08.540
And then the camera pans past him and he has just cut out the back of his desk chair.
然后镜头扫过他，他刚刚把办公椅的靠背剪了下来。

314
00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:11.220
That's mesh into like a circle.
剪成了一个圆形的网状物。

315
00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:12.600
And he's like, who's going to volunteer?
他说，谁愿意自告奋勇？

316
00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:13.780
This is going to be great.
这一定会很棒。

317
00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.660
It's like, wait, portable, reusable.
他说，便携、可重复使用。

318
00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:17.380
You could just put it in your dishwasher.
你甚至可以直接放进洗碗机里洗。

319
00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:18.280
So what?
那又怎样？

320
00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:22.480
He's going to start using the bathroom through this meshy cover, but he's thrilled.
他打算隔着这个网罩上厕所，但他兴奋极了。

321
00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:25.580
He thinks he's going to be a gazillionaire with the mesh toilet guard.
他觉得靠这个网状马桶防护罩他能成为亿万富翁。

322
00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.120
I don't know where to begin.
我不知道该从何说起。

323
00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:28.080
I know.
我知道。

324
00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:31.200
So that was the cold open that they didn't end up using.
所以这就是他们最终没用的开场戏。

325
00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.460
And they just jumped right into the episode.
他们直接跳进了正片。

326
00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:34.680
Here's the thing.
问题是这样的。

327
00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:38.820
I can't remember if we shot that, but I remember that joke.
我不记得我们是否拍过那个片段，但我记得那个笑话。

328
00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:42.180
Probably from the table read, cause we must've read it.
可能是剧本围读时听到的，因为我们肯定读过。

329
00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:42.540
Yeah.
是的。

330
00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:46.940
I remember the joke that Michael threw his keys in out of anger.
我记得迈克尔因为生气把钥匙扔进马桶的那个笑话。

331
00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:49.020
That was my favorite part.
那是我的最爱。

332
00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:50.980
So this isn't in the deleted scenes then.
所以这不在删减片段里。

333
00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:55.340
It's not in the deleted scenes, but it is in the script, but they didn't use it.
不在删减片段里，但在剧本里，只是他们没用。

334
00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:56.140
Hmm.
嗯。

335
00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:57.820
Just a little trivia for you.
给你提供一点小花絮。

336
00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.700
Since I have the script, the script is paying off already.
既然我有剧本，剧本已经派上用场了。

337
00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.400
I'm excited about it.
我很兴奋。

338
00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:08.160
The way this episode does start is Michael comes out of his office.
这一集的开头是迈克尔从办公室走出来。

339
00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.840
He's dressed in his jeans.
他穿着牛仔裤。

340
00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:11.680
Yeah.
是的。

341
00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:13.140
It's got sneakers on.
还穿着运动鞋。

342
00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:14.480
He's trying to look young and hip.
他想让自己看起来年轻时髦。

343
00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:15.640
I think so.
我也这么觉得。

344
00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:19.460
Pam and Oscar and Daryl are all around reception.
帕姆、奥斯卡和达里尔都在前台附近。

345
00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:25.880
And we find out that today, the four of them will be attending the job fair at Valley View
我们发现今天他们四个人要去山景高中参加招聘会，

346
00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:30.620
High School in search of new interns, because he wants to euthanize the office.
寻找新实习生，因为他想给办公室“安乐死”。

347
00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:36.460
Well, there is a deleted scene where Michael shares that he's been really depressed since
其实有一个删减片段，迈克尔分享说自从

348
00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:37.200
Ryan left.
瑞安离开后他一直很抑郁。

349
00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:38.680
Sam, can you play that?
萨姆，你能播放一下吗？

350
00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:41.140
Depressed.
抑郁。

351
00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:44.660
Ever since Ryan left, I've been going through empty nest syndrome.
自从瑞安离开后，我就一直患有空巢综合征。

352
00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:50.300
And I call it that because that's the way I felt when empty nest went off the air.
我之所以这么叫，是因为《空巢》停播时我就是这种感觉。

353
00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:53.120
I am lonely.
我很寂寞。

354
00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:55.860
And I need a new Ryan.
我需要一个新的瑞安。

355
00:14:58.470 --> 00:14:59.370
That's amazing.
那太棒了。

356
00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:00.150
Yeah.
是啊。

357
00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:06.830
And so he sees this job fair at the local high school as his way to recruit some young buddy.
所以他把当地高中的招聘会看作是招募年轻伙伴的机会。

358
00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.750
Michael just wants a younger sibling.
迈克尔只是想要个弟弟妹妹。

359
00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:09.570
Yeah.
是啊。

360
00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:12.190
We had a fan question from Thomas V.
我们收到了一位粉丝托马斯·V的提问。

361
00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:15.750
How did they decide who got to go to the job fair?
他们是怎么决定谁去参加招聘会的？

362
00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:20.810
This was one of those instances where they would look at the cast and they would say,
这属于那种他们会审视演员阵容，然后说：

363
00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:24.390
who haven't we seen together yet or in a while?
我们还没见过谁和谁搭档，或者谁很久没一起出现了？

364
00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:27.410
And that's kind of how they pulled the names.
他们就是这样选人的。

365
00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:33.630
Because something I noticed is that there is not technically a salesperson represented.
因为我注意到，严格来说并没有销售人员代表参加。

366
00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.090
So there's someone from accounting.
所以有会计部的人。

367
00:15:36.090 --> 00:15:41.410
There's someone from the warehouse front reception who Michael refers to as the eye candy.
还有前台接待，迈克尔称她为“养眼美女”。

368
00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:46.170
And Michael, who I guess could also cover sales.
还有迈克尔，我想他也可以代表销售部。

369
00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:46.870
Right.
没错。

370
00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:48.210
He was a really good salesman.
他确实是个非常出色的销售员。

371
00:15:48.370 --> 00:15:48.950
He was.
他确实是。

372
00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:49.410
Yeah.
是啊。

373
00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:56.070
But yeah, this was more about pairing of people and characters and who would make a great foil
但确实，这更多是关于人物角色的搭配，以及谁能成为迈克尔在招聘会上的绝佳陪衬。

374
00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:57.950
for Michael at the job fair.
对于迈克尔在招聘会上的表现。

375
00:15:58.190 --> 00:15:59.830
Well, we know why I couldn't go.
好吧，我们知道我为什么不能去。

376
00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:00.350
Yeah.
是啊。

377
00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.850
You would have just to shoot four floating heads.
你当时只能拍到四个漂浮的脑袋。

378
00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:09.670
It would have just been four heads in a high school auditorium because I was super pregs.
那画面里只会是高中礼堂里的四个脑袋，因为我当时怀孕了。

379
00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:11.770
OK, so that's who went to the high school.
好的，这就是去高中参加招聘会的人员。

380
00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:15.490
But now we have this other kind of odd pairing headed to the golf course.
但现在我们还有另一组奇怪的搭档要去高尔夫球场。

381
00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:17.230
It's Jim, Andy and Kevin.
是吉姆、安迪和凯文。

382
00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:19.130
And Jim's on probation.
而且吉姆还在留职察看期。

383
00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:21.190
He's got to make this big, big sale.
他必须完成这笔大单子。

384
00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:24.390
And this is his ragtag team that I guess is going to help him.
而这就是我猜想会帮他的那支乌合之众小队。

385
00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:25.110
Yeah.
是啊。

386
00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:26.890
Things start off a little.
事情开始得有点……

387
00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:28.650
How would you put it?
该怎么形容呢？

388
00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:35.250
Oddly, because the first thing that Andy does is insult Mr. McGuire, their potential
很奇怪，因为安迪做的第一件事就是侮辱他们的潜在客户麦奎尔先生，

389
00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:38.070
client, because he's wearing a Dartmouth sweatshirt.
因为他穿着达特茅斯学院的运动衫。

390
00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:42.910
He tells him to take it off and that his grandfather would be spinning in his urn if he knew he was,
他叫他脱掉，还说如果他爷爷知道他在和达特茅斯的校友打高尔夫，

391
00:16:42.930 --> 00:16:44.630
you know, golfing with a Dartmouth alum.
你知道的，他爷爷会在骨灰盒里气得打转。

392
00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:48.230
There's clearly some real rivalry here between Cornell and Dartmouth.
康奈尔大学和达特茅斯学院之间显然存在真正的竞争。

393
00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:49.530
Well, I looked it up.
嗯，我查了一下。

394
00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:58.010
It's this big college football rivalry between the Cornell Big Red and the Dartmouth Big Green.
这是康奈尔大红队和达特茅斯大绿队之间的一场大型大学橄榄球竞争。

395
00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:02.990
I guess these two schools were major football powers back in the day.
我猜这两所学校在过去都是橄榄球强校。

396
00:17:03.150 --> 00:17:07.070
There's since been a split in the divisions, the football divisions.
后来橄榄球赛区进行了拆分。

397
00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:11.570
But prior to the split, Cornell kind of dominated the national championships.
但在拆分之前，康奈尔在全国锦标赛中占据主导地位。

398
00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:17.910
They won in 1915, 1921, 22, 23, and 39.
他们在1915年、1921年、1922年、1923年和1939年都赢了。

399
00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:21.350
Dartmouth won once in 1925.
达特茅斯只在1925年赢过一次。

400
00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:24.050
So Cornell was dominating the Ivy League.
所以康奈尔曾经统治过常春藤联盟。

401
00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:24.770
Yes.
是的。

402
00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:29.390
But then in 1940, there was this infamous game, Ange.
但在1940年，发生了一场臭名昭著的比赛，安吉。

403
00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:30.050
Oh.
哦。

404
00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:32.750
Cornell had a 16-game winning streak.
康奈尔大学当时保持着16连胜的纪录。

405
00:17:32.870 --> 00:17:34.750
And this was like a school record.
这算是学校的纪录了。

406
00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:39.330
They were about to win the national championship with a score of 7-3.
他们当时以7比3的比分即将赢得全国冠军。

407
00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:40.990
But guess what they did?
但你猜他们做了什么？

408
00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:41.650
What?
什么？

409
00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:50.510
They did a film review of the game and found out that Cornell had inadvertently used five downs instead of four.
他们回看了比赛录像，发现康奈尔大学无意中用了五次进攻机会，而不是四次。

410
00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:53.190
And they had to forfeit the game to Dartmouth.
结果他们不得不把比赛判负给达特茅斯学院。

411
00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:54.290
Oh.
哦。

412
00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:58.350
According to the ESPN College Football Encyclopedia,
根据ESPN大学橄榄球百科全书的记载，

413
00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:02.970
they consider this to be the second greatest moment in college football history.
他们认为这是大学橄榄球史上第二伟大的时刻。

414
00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:07.490
And it is commonly referred to as the fifth down game.
它通常被称为“第五次进攻”比赛。

415
00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:08.470
Hmm.
嗯。

416
00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:13.610
So I guess that's why Andy's grandfather was spinning in his urn.
所以我猜这就是为什么安迪的祖父在骨灰盒里都要气得打转了。

417
00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:17.410
Well, Mindy went to Dartmouth, so she might have known some of that rivalry.
嗯，明迪是达特茅斯毕业的，所以她可能了解一些这种竞争关系。

418
00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:20.230
I have to think that might have come up in the writer's room.
我觉得这可能在编剧室里被讨论过。

419
00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:21.050
I wonder.
我也在想。

420
00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:23.610
And there are deleted scenes that support this.
而且有一些删减片段支持这一点。

421
00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:25.750
Jim shares that, you know what?
吉姆分享说，你知道吗？

422
00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:32.430
He's bringing Andy on purpose because he knew Andy would flip out about Mr. McGuire being a Dartmouth guy.
他带安迪来是故意的，因为他知道安迪听到麦奎尔先生是达特茅斯的人会抓狂。

423
00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:39.350
And then they would have sort of this like common enemy that it would be bonding for Mr. McGuire and Jim because Andy's an idiot.
然后他们就会有一个共同的敌人，这会让麦奎尔先生和吉姆建立联系，因为安迪是个白痴。

424
00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:45.970
Well, that doesn't track because Jim seems so horrified by Andy's comment to Mr. McGuire.
嗯，这说不通，因为吉姆看起来对安迪对麦奎尔先生的评论感到非常震惊。

425
00:18:46.570 --> 00:18:47.050
Exactly.
没错。

426
00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:51.490
So then there's this scene where, you know, Mr. McGuire's like, gosh, this guy.
所以后来有这么一个场景，麦奎尔先生说，天哪，这家伙。

427
00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:53.490
And Jim's like, I know, Cornell, right?
然后吉姆说，我知道，康奈尔，对吧？

428
00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:55.030
Oh, I get it.
哦，我明白了。

429
00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:55.870
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

430
00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:57.870
Jim was being diabolical.
吉姆真是太阴险了。

431
00:18:58.150 --> 00:18:59.310
He had a whole plan.
他有一个完整的计划。

432
00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:00.270
Right.
对。

433
00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.030
Best friends through a common enemy.
通过共同的敌人成为最好的朋友。

434
00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:04.230
That's right.
没错。

435
00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:05.130
Look at us.
看看我们。

436
00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:05.850
We're buddies now.
我们现在是哥们儿了。

437
00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:06.410
We're pals.
我们是好朋友。

438
00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:07.170
Give me your business.
把你的生意交给我吧。

439
00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:09.170
Don't pay attention to that Cornell idiot.
别理那个康奈尔的白痴。

440
00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:10.790
Thank God you have me here.
谢天谢地你还有我在这里。

441
00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:11.390
Yeah.
是的。

442
00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:14.330
Don't pay attention to that idiot who also works at my company.
别理那个也在我公司工作的白痴。

443
00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:16.690
I don't know if this was a great plan, Jim.
我不知道这算不算一个好计划，吉姆。

444
00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:19.570
Well, part of his strategy.
嗯，这是他策略的一部分。

445
00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:24.430
Andy also can't shake hands with Mr. McGuire because his hands are covered in blisters.
安迪也没法和麦奎尔先生握手，因为他的手上全是水泡。

446
00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:25.750
Blisties.
水泡泡。

447
00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:26.350
Yeah.
是的。

448
00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:27.750
He's nifty gifties.
他真是个花哨的小可爱。

449
00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:28.670
He's blisties.
他满手水泡。

450
00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:31.310
He loves a little IES on things.
他喜欢给东西加个“IES”后缀。

451
00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:34.170
I got the lowdown on how they made those blisters.
我打听到了他们是怎么做出那些水泡的。

452
00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:35.650
Oh, let's hear it.
哦，说来听听。

453
00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:36.330
Who did it?
是谁做的？

454
00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:38.150
It was our makeup artist, Laverne.
是我们的化妆师拉弗恩。

455
00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:39.250
She applied the makeup.
她负责上妆。

456
00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:42.890
It took her about 20 or 30 minutes to do it.
她花了大概二三十分钟才弄好。

457
00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:46.350
She started by putting coloring on his hands.
她先是在他手上涂了颜色。

458
00:19:46.530 --> 00:19:48.170
So she kind of painted his hands red.
所以她算是把他的手涂成了红色。

459
00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:52.370
Then she covered it with something called RCMA scar making material.
然后她用一种叫RCMA的疤痕制作材料覆盖在上面。

460
00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:57.070
She said it's really, really tricky to apply because as soon as it dries, it's set.
她说这东西非常非常难涂，因为一旦干了就定型了。

461
00:19:57.310 --> 00:19:59.270
You can't move it and it dries really, really faSt.
你没法再调整，而且它干得非常非常快。

462
00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:04.310
So she would put it on really quickly with a tiny metal spatula and tweezers.
所以她得用一把小金属刮刀和镊子飞快地涂上去。

463
00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:08.650
And that afterwards, Ed was not allowed to wash his hands or get them wet.
而且在那之后，艾德就不被允许洗手或弄湿手了。

464
00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:10.330
How'd he go to the bathroom?
那他怎么上厕所？

465
00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:16.530
I mean, I guess he just didn't wash his hands after.
我是说，我猜他上完厕所后只是没洗手而已。

466
00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:23.150
I hope he didn't awkward get them wet in any other way.
我希望他没在其他情况下尴尬地弄湿手。

467
00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:26.570
Do you always wash your hands after you go to the bathroom?
你上完厕所总是洗手吗？

468
00:20:27.230 --> 00:20:27.510
Yes.
是的。

469
00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:28.810
Even at home?
在家里也洗吗？

470
00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:29.650
Yes.
是的。

471
00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:33.750
After you pee at home, you wash your hands with soap and water every time?
你在家小便后，每次都会用肥皂和水洗手吗？

472
00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:34.950
Every time.
每次都洗。

473
