安吉拉，我们拍这些场景时真的太开心了。

630
00:27:17.480 --> 00:27:21.200
I so loved getting to be on location with these three guys.
我非常喜欢和这三个人一起在外景地拍摄。

631
00:27:21.460 --> 00:27:23.300
We had the best time.
我们玩得最开心了。

632
00:27:23.640 --> 00:27:28.980
They gave all the background actors the direction that they should be like having a great time
他们给所有的背景演员下达了指令，要求他们在其他展位表现得非常开心、

633
00:27:28.980 --> 00:27:33.920
and smiling and high energy at all the other booths so that when you got to ours, it was
面带微笑、充满活力，这样当你们走到我们这里时，就会显得

634
00:27:33.920 --> 00:27:35.840
particularly quiet and sad looking.
格外冷清和凄凉。

635
00:27:36.360 --> 00:27:38.100
It really, really works.
效果真的非常好。

636
00:27:38.300 --> 00:27:39.720
It was cracking me up.
我当时快笑死了。

637
00:27:40.060 --> 00:27:43.780
Should we go back over to Dunder Mifflin and see what everyone else is up to?
我们要回到邓德·米夫林看看其他人都在忙什么吗？

638
00:27:44.200 --> 00:27:44.640
Yes.
好啊。

639
00:27:44.800 --> 00:27:46.400
Well, let me tell you what they're up to.
好吧，让我告诉你他们在忙什么。

640
00:27:46.520 --> 00:27:48.000
They're up to trying to sneak out of work.
他们在忙着想溜出公司。

641
00:27:48.240 --> 00:27:50.340
I mean, Meredith and Phyllis are stirring the pot.
我是说，梅雷迪思和菲利斯在煽风点火。

642
00:27:50.580 --> 00:27:51.400
Michael is gone.
迈克尔不在。

643
00:27:51.600 --> 00:27:53.100
They don't want to stay the whole day.
他们不想待上一整天。

644
00:27:53.440 --> 00:27:53.760
No.
没错。

645
00:27:53.760 --> 00:27:58.360
And Creed has a great line where he says he finished his work months ago.
克里德有一句很棒的台词，他说他几个月前就做完工作了。

646
00:27:58.580 --> 00:27:59.640
I loved that.
我太喜欢那句了。

647
00:28:00.100 --> 00:28:01.260
Like, what is he doing?
就像是，他到底在干什么？

648
00:28:02.060 --> 00:28:05.560
Dwight reminds them all that when Michael is gone, Jim is in charge.
德怀特提醒他们所有人，迈克尔不在时，吉姆负责。

649
00:28:05.760 --> 00:28:07.780
And when Jim is gone, Andy and Dwight are in charge.
而吉姆不在时，安迪和德怀特负责。

650
00:28:07.940 --> 00:28:10.740
And when Andy is gone, you answer to Dwight.
如果安迪也不在，那你就得听德怀特的。

651
00:28:11.020 --> 00:28:13.000
And Stanley's like, I don't give a crap.
然后斯坦利就像是说，我才不在乎呢。

652
00:28:13.140 --> 00:28:13.500
I'm out.
我走了。

653
00:28:13.700 --> 00:28:17.040
I love so much that moment when Stanley walks out the door.
我特别喜欢斯坦利走出门口的那一刻。

654
00:28:17.340 --> 00:28:17.980
I do too.
我也是。

655
00:28:18.140 --> 00:28:19.700
And Dwight doesn't know what to do.
而德怀特却不知所措。

656
00:28:19.880 --> 00:28:22.820
You know, we have said we feel like Stanley is the person Dwight is like,
你知道，我们曾说我们觉得斯坦利是那种让德怀特觉得，

657
00:28:22.820 --> 00:28:25.080
I am not going to, like, mess with Stanley.
我还是别去招惹斯坦利比较好的人。

658
00:28:25.380 --> 00:28:31.480
But Dwight asserts to the whole office, look, you guys, the American workday ends at five
但德怀特向整个办公室宣称，听着，各位，美国的工作日是在五点钟结束的。

659
00:28:31.480 --> 00:28:32.020
o'clock.
所以你们必须待到工作日结束，没商量。

660
00:28:32.260 --> 00:28:36.120
And so you must stay until the end of the workday, period.
否则我就去告发你们。

661
00:28:36.520 --> 00:28:37.980
Or I'll tattle on you.
没错。

662
00:28:38.480 --> 00:28:38.720
Right.
回到高中，帕姆正在和一个年轻的准实习生聊天。

663
00:28:40.100 --> 00:28:44.120
Back at the high school, Pam is chatting up a young prospective intern.
他其实对邓德·米夫林公司挺感兴趣的。

664
00:28:44.640 --> 00:28:47.680
He's actually interested in Dunder Mifflin.
然后迈克尔示意她停下。

665
00:28:47.820 --> 00:28:50.540
And Michael signals her to stop.
是啊。

666
00:28:50.840 --> 00:28:51.160
Yeah.
嗯，不仅仅是那样。

667
00:28:51.420 --> 00:28:52.560
Well, not just that.
他走到这个名叫贾斯汀的孩子面前。

668
00:28:52.560 --> 00:28:54.760
But he goes up to this kid whose name is Justin.
他说，我觉得这份工作不适合你。

669
00:28:55.140 --> 00:28:57.580
He says, I don't think this is the job for you.
造纸对你来说应该更像是一种爱好。

670
00:28:57.800 --> 00:28:59.760
Paper should be more of a hobby for you.
然后他拿走了那个孩子正在看的宣传册。

671
00:29:00.040 --> 00:29:03.380
And then he takes away the kid's pamphlet that he was looking at.
是啊。

672
00:29:03.720 --> 00:29:04.020
Yeah.
不过，我们收到了一条来自Harmjen V和Alyssa C的粉丝发现。

673
00:29:04.200 --> 00:29:08.760
We had a fan catch about it, though, from Harmjen V and Alyssa C.
如果迈克尔去招聘会只带了一张纸，那帕姆给贾斯汀、后来又被迈克尔拿走的那本宣传册是从哪儿来的？

674
00:29:08.760 --> 00:29:18.260
If Michael only brought one sheet of paper to the job fair, where did the brochure come from that Pam gave to Justin and Michael took away?
嗯。

675
00:29:18.960 --> 00:29:19.420
Hmm.
好问题。

676
00:29:20.020 --> 00:29:20.540
Good question.
我的意思是，很明显他们带了宣传册。

677
00:29:20.780 --> 00:29:22.680
I mean, clearly they brought a brochure.
我觉得那张纸是他们的道具，是那种当人们走过时用来吸引眼球的东西。

678
00:29:22.920 --> 00:29:28.760
I felt like the paper was their prop, was the thing that was supposed to be the eye-catching moment as people walked by.
所以也许在桌子底下，帕姆还有一些额外的资料。

679
00:29:28.760 --> 00:29:32.300
So maybe under the desk, Pam had some additional materials.
当那张纸让你停下脚步去和他们展位的人交谈时，你就能拿到宣传册了。

680
00:29:32.660 --> 00:29:39.360
When the paper makes you stop in your tracks to talk to these people at their booth, then you get a pamphlet.
好吧。

681
00:29:39.360 --> 00:29:40.220
Okay.
我喜欢这个解释。

682
00:29:40.440 --> 00:29:41.080
I like it.
迈克尔对贾斯汀在他们的空白纸上签名感到愤怒。

683
00:29:41.860 --> 00:29:47.440
Michael is furious that Justin signed his name on their blank piece of paper.
当得知帕姆只带了那一页纸时，他更生气了。

684
00:29:47.660 --> 00:29:51.520
He's even more furious to learn that Pam only brought the one.
是啊。

685
00:29:51.980 --> 00:29:52.340
Yeah.
而帕姆就像是说，不好意思？

686
00:29:52.440 --> 00:29:54.360
And Pam's like, excuse me?
我喜欢她完全当面拆穿他的样子。

687
00:29:54.900 --> 00:29:56.820
I love that she totally calls him out on it.
我知道。

688
00:29:57.040 --> 00:29:57.620
I know.
她说，迈克尔，你不记得了吗？

689
00:29:57.880 --> 00:30:00.060
She said, Michael, do you not remember?
我说，你确定我们只需要一张纸吗？

690
00:30:00.540 --> 00:30:04.880
I said, are you sure that we only need one sheet of paper?
你说，是的，我们只需要一张纸就能有所作为。

691
00:30:05.360 --> 00:30:08.620
And you said, yeah, we only need one sheet of paper to make a difference.
然后你对着我的茶打了个喷嚏，还说，别担心，只是过敏。

692
00:30:08.840 --> 00:30:12.620
And then you sneezed in my tea and said, don't worry, it's just allergies.
帕姆，证据确凿。

693
00:30:13.400 --> 00:30:14.860
Pam, with the receipts.
现在的年轻人都这么说，珍娜。

694
00:30:15.240 --> 00:30:16.500
That's what the kids say, Jenna.
哦，我喜欢这个说法。

695
00:30:16.880 --> 00:30:17.580
Oh, I like it.
我们收到一个来自凯特·B的粉丝提问。

696
00:30:18.140 --> 00:30:20.000
We had a fan question from Kate B.
当贾斯汀在纸上签名时，他写的是贾斯汀·E。

697
00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:24.160
When Justin signs his name on the piece of paper, he writes Justin E.
但后来在剧集中，他告诉迈克尔他的姓是保尔斯尼克。

698
00:30:24.440 --> 00:30:29.240
But later in the episode, he tells Michael that his last name is Paul Snick.
解释一下。

699
00:30:29.640 --> 00:30:30.260
Explain.
嗯。

700
00:30:30.840 --> 00:30:31.100
Hmm.
嗯。

701
00:30:31.360 --> 00:30:32.240
I'll tell you.
我来告诉你。

702
00:30:32.420 --> 00:30:33.520
I am intrigued.
我很有兴趣。

703
00:30:33.900 --> 00:30:39.420
The actor who plays Justin, his name is Trevor Einhorn.
饰演贾斯汀的演员，他的名字叫特雷弗·艾因霍恩。

704
00:30:39.840 --> 00:30:42.580
Oh, so maybe he was writing his actual last name.
哦，所以他写的可能是他真实的姓氏。

705
00:30:42.880 --> 00:30:43.520
Yes.
是的。

706
00:30:43.740 --> 00:30:44.560
Isn't that amazing?
这不是很神奇吗？

707
00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:45.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

708
00:30:45.340 --> 00:30:50.380
So Trevor Einhorn has been a professional actor since he was five years old.
特雷弗·艾因霍恩从五岁起就是一名职业演员了。

709
00:30:50.560 --> 00:30:55.260
And his breakout role was on the television comedy, Frasier.
他成名的角色是在喜剧《欢乐一家亲》中。

710
00:30:55.480 --> 00:31:00.080
He played Frederick Crane, the son of Frasier and Lilith.
他饰演了弗雷泽和莉莉丝的儿子弗雷德里克·克莱恩。

711
00:31:00.300 --> 00:31:01.760
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

712
00:31:01.960 --> 00:31:02.400
Yes.
是的。

713
00:31:02.680 --> 00:31:05.660
He also went on to have a recurring role on Mad Men.
后来他还在《广告狂人》中担任常驻角色。

714
00:31:05.840 --> 00:31:08.700
He was in season six and seven as a copywriter.
他在第六季和第七季中饰演一名文案撰稿人。

715
00:31:08.700 --> 00:31:13.680
And he also played Neil Kellerman in the ABC remake of Dirty Dancing.
他还曾在ABC翻拍的《辣身舞》中饰演尼尔·凯勒曼。

716
00:31:14.340 --> 00:31:14.620
Hmm.
嗯。

717
00:31:14.860 --> 00:31:19.020
He currently stars as Josh Hoberman in the sci-fi show The Magicians.
他目前在科幻剧《魔法师》中饰演乔什·霍伯曼。

718
00:31:19.300 --> 00:31:20.640
He is a Scorpio.
他是天蝎座的。

719
00:31:20.780 --> 00:31:21.720
I'll have you know.
我得让你知道这一点。

720
00:31:22.080 --> 00:31:23.260
That's new for a gueSt.
这对嘉宾来说是新鲜事。

721
00:31:23.340 --> 00:31:26.180
I don't feel like you've shared their zodiac sign before.
我觉得你以前没分享过他们的星座。

722
00:31:26.420 --> 00:31:28.460
Is this a new part of the guest star breakdown?
这是嘉宾介绍的新环节吗？

723
00:31:28.940 --> 00:31:31.500
Well, it showed up in his bio, so I thought I'd throw it in there.
嗯，这出现在他的简介里，所以我想顺便提一下。

724
00:31:31.760 --> 00:31:31.940
Okay.
好吧。

725
00:31:31.940 --> 00:31:37.140
Finally, he is not related to our cinematographer, Randall Einhorn.
最后，他和我们的摄影指导兰德尔·艾因霍恩没有亲戚关系。

726
00:31:37.360 --> 00:31:38.340
That is correct.
没错。

727
00:31:38.540 --> 00:31:39.760
Just a coincidence.
只是巧合而已。

728
00:31:40.560 --> 00:31:43.980
Everyone back in the bullpen still really wants to sneak out.
办公室里的每个人都真的很想溜走。

729
00:31:44.280 --> 00:31:45.740
They've waited for their moment.
他们一直在等时机。

730
00:31:45.960 --> 00:31:49.680
Dwight finally gets up and exits the bullpen to go to the bathroom.
德怀特终于起身离开办公室去洗手间了。

731
00:31:50.120 --> 00:31:52.600
And Creed calls Angela to tell her they're all leaving.
克里德给安吉拉打电话，告诉她他们都要走了。

732
00:31:52.940 --> 00:31:57.820
This scene made me laugh so hard, Jenna, because this is a bit that Creed and I still do.
这一幕让我笑得好大声，珍娜，因为这是克里德和我至今还在玩的梗。

733
00:31:57.820 --> 00:32:02.160
To this day, Creed will text me, Pumpkin's out.
直到今天，克里德还会给我发短信说：“南瓜走了”。

734
00:32:02.660 --> 00:32:05.060
Or if we hang out, I'm like, all right, Creed, I'm going to go.
或者如果我们一起出去玩，我会说，好了，克里德，我要走了。

735
00:32:05.220 --> 00:32:06.260
He'll say, Pumpkin's out.
他会说：“南瓜走了”。

736
00:32:06.400 --> 00:32:09.960
Like, he still says this to me after all of these years.
这么多年过去了，他还是会对我这么说。

737
00:32:10.360 --> 00:32:12.560
And this just warmed my heart.
这真的让我的心感到温暖。

738
00:32:12.760 --> 00:32:13.620
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢这一幕了。

739
00:32:13.740 --> 00:32:14.780
Sam, can you play the clip?
萨姆，能播放一下片段吗？

740
00:32:19.510 --> 00:32:20.310
Extension 128.
分机128。

741
00:32:20.690 --> 00:32:21.410
Hiya, Pumpkin.
嗨，南瓜。

742
00:32:21.410 --> 00:32:21.890
It's Creed.
我是克里德。

743
00:32:22.550 --> 00:32:23.850
Say we're going to ditch this bitch.
我们要甩掉那个臭婆娘。

744
00:32:24.090 --> 00:32:24.510
You in?
你加入吗？

745
00:32:25.110 --> 00:32:25.510
No.
不。

746
00:32:25.770 --> 00:32:26.310
Are you out?
你要退出吗？

747
00:32:28.830 --> 00:32:29.430
Pumpkin's out.
南瓜退出了。

748
00:32:29.590 --> 00:32:30.170
Let's go, gang.
走吧，伙计们。

749
00:32:31.150 --> 00:32:34.270
We got so much mail about this scene, Angela.
安吉拉，我们收到了很多关于这一幕的来信。

750
00:32:34.650 --> 00:32:39.350
People who listen to the podcast know that Creed calls you Pumpkin in real life.
听播客的人都知道，克里德在现实生活中叫你南瓜。

751
00:32:39.410 --> 00:32:45.150
And they wanted to know, was Creed ad-libbing in the scene and using his real life nickname
他们想知道，克里德在这一幕里是即兴发挥，用了他现实生活中的绰号

752
00:32:45.150 --> 00:32:45.750
for you?
来称呼你吗？

753
00:32:45.910 --> 00:32:47.970
Or was Pumpkin in the script?
还是说剧本里就写了“南瓜”这个词？

754
00:32:48.230 --> 00:32:50.490
And then he started calling you Pumpkin after this.
而且从那以后他就开始叫你“南瓜”了。

755
00:32:50.730 --> 00:32:53.490
This scene is exactly as it is in the script.
这一幕和剧本里写的一模一样。

756
00:32:53.750 --> 00:32:54.190
Exactly.
没错。

757
00:32:54.650 --> 00:32:56.610
So Creed did not improvise that.
所以克里德并不是即兴发挥的。

758
00:32:56.610 --> 00:33:01.030
But I will tell you, ever since we shot Job Fair, he has called me Pumpkin.
但我得告诉你，自从我们拍完“招聘会”那一集，他就一直叫我“南瓜”。

759
00:33:01.170 --> 00:33:03.050
To this day, he still calls me Pumpkin.
直到今天，他还是叫我“南瓜”。

760
00:33:03.350 --> 00:33:04.450
That is so cute.
太可爱了。

761
00:33:04.690 --> 00:33:05.290
I know.
我知道。

762
00:33:05.290 --> 00:33:06.210
It's so cute.
真的太可爱了。

763
00:33:06.490 --> 00:33:07.710
I loved that scene.
我很喜欢那一幕。

764
00:33:08.150 --> 00:33:12.010
Well, now Dwight comes out of the restroom and he sees that everyone has left.
好了，现在德怀特从洗手间出来，发现大家都走了。

765
00:33:13.310 --> 00:33:14.770
Everyone except Angela.
除了安吉拉以外的所有人。

766
00:33:15.430 --> 00:33:15.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

767
00:33:16.070 --> 00:33:19.390
Which makes total sense because she's the one other rule follower in this group.
这完全说得通，因为她是这群人里另一个遵守规则的人。

768
00:33:19.970 --> 00:33:20.310
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

769
00:33:20.310 --> 00:33:26.530
There is a great scene that's deleted where Dwight comes out and he goes, ha, last man standing.
有一段很棒的删减片段，德怀特出来后说，哈，最后剩下的人。

770
00:33:26.830 --> 00:33:30.150
And then Angela briskly walks past him and goes, excuse me.
然后安吉拉快步走过他身边说，借过。

771
00:33:30.630 --> 00:33:35.570
And then there's a talking head that Angela has that really explains why she is just as
接着安吉拉有一个采访镜头，真正解释了为什么她也

772
00:33:35.570 --> 00:33:39.030
eager to be one of the last people in the office.
那么渴望成为办公室里最后走的人之一。

773
00:33:40.570 --> 00:33:44.190
Whenever I'm here by myself, I like to pretend that all the others are dead.
每当我独自待在这里时，我喜欢假装其他人都死了。

774
00:33:45.610 --> 00:33:46.890
So this is nice.
所以这样挺好的。

775
00:33:49.870 --> 00:33:50.690
Baby, laugh out loud.
天哪，笑死我了。

776
00:33:50.730 --> 00:33:51.610
I spit out my water.
我把喝的水都喷出来了。

777
00:33:51.610 --> 00:33:54.830
I went to take a sip of water while we were listening to the deleted scene.
我们听删减片段的时候，我正想喝口水。

778
00:33:54.830 --> 00:33:57.010
It seemed like a safe time to take a sip of water.
本来觉得那是喝水的好时机。

779
00:33:57.310 --> 00:33:59.350
But that, that was so good.
但那段真的太棒了。

780
00:33:59.710 --> 00:34:01.550
She pretends that everyone is dead.
她假装所有人都死了。

781
00:34:01.670 --> 00:34:04.010
And at the end, they had me do a little smile like that.
最后他们让我露出了那样一个小小的微笑。

782
00:34:04.130 --> 00:34:05.570
